  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# \ud83d\ude80 Amazon ML Challenge 2026: Business Entity Resolution\n",
        "## High-Performance Execution on Google Colab (Pro / AI Pro)\n",
        "\n",
        "This notebook orchestrates the complete, end-to-end execution of the offline Business Entity Resolution system on the **full competition dataset** (~2.2M train S1, ~10.3M train targets, ~1.73M test S1, ~10M test targets).\n",
        "\n",
        "### \ud83d\udca1 Why Colab Pro / Google AI Pro?\n",
        "- **High-RAM CPU Runtime**: Provides **~52 GB RAM** and **8\u201316 vCPUs**.\n",
        "- **Fast NVMe Disk**: ~150\u2013225 GB free disk space.\n",
        "- **Parallel Speed**: With `configs/cloud.json` (`8` feature extraction workers, `16` LightGBM threads), the full inference on ~86M candidate pairs runs in **~1.5 to 2 hours** (compared to 15+ hours on a laptop).\n",
        "\n",
        "> **Colab Setup Tip**:\n",
        "> Go to **Runtime** > **Change runtime type** > Select **CPU** with **High-RAM** enabled. (GPU is not required since the pipeline is CPU-optimized with multi-threaded RapidFuzz, DuckDB, and LightGBM)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "### 1. Check Hardware & System Resources\n",
        "Let's confirm the CPU cores, RAM, and disk space available in this session."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "import os, psutil, shutil\n",
        "\n",
        "ram_gb = psutil.virtual_memory().total / (1024**3)\n",
        "cpu_count = os.cpu_count()\n",
        "disk_gb = shutil.disk_usage(\"/\").free / (1024**3)\n",
        "\n",
        "print(f\"RAM available: {ram_gb:.2f} GB\")\n",
        "print(f\"CPU cores / threads: {cpu_count}\")\n",
        "print(f\"Disk space available: {disk_gb:.2f} GB\")\n",
        "\n",
        "if ram_gb < 25:\n",
        "    print(\"\u26a0\ufe0f Notice: Standard RAM detected. Recommended: Runtime -> Change runtime type -> High-RAM.\")\n",
        "else:\n",
        "    print(\"\u2705 High-RAM instance active! Ready for full-scale processing.\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "### 2. Setup Project Files in Colab\n",
        "You have two options to load your project into Colab:\n",
        "- **Option A (Recommended)**: Mount Google Drive and unzip `aws_challenge_colab.zip` directly.\n",
        "- **Option B**: Upload `aws_challenge_colab.zip` to Colab's file browser and unzip it."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# Option A: Mount Google Drive (Uncomment if using Google Drive)\n",
        "# from google.colab import drive\n",
        "# drive.mount('/content/drive')\n",
        "# !cp /content/drive/MyDrive/aws_challenge_colab.zip /content/aws_challenge_colab.zip\n",
        "\n",
        "# Unzip project archive into Colab local disk (/content/)\n",
        "!unzip -q -o /content/aws_challenge_colab.zip -d /content/\n",
        "%cd /content\n",
        "!ls -lh"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "### 3. Install Required Dependencies\n",
        "Install the pinned high-performance libraries (DuckDB, RapidFuzz, LightGBM, PyArrow, etc.)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "!pip install -q -r code/business_entity_resolution/requirements.txt\n",
        "!pip install -q pytest"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "### 4. Run Verification Test Suite\n",
        "Run all 15 unit and integration tests to ensure deterministic metric calculation, script handling, and multi-process pipelines work in this environment."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "!python -m pytest code/business_entity_resolution/tests -v"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "### 5. Generate Hardware-Adaptive Configuration\n",
        "This cell detects your instance's exact RAM and CPU count and generates `configs/colab_auto.json` tailored to maximize performance without hitting OOM limits."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "import os, psutil, json\n",
        "from pathlib import Path\n",
        "\n",
        "ram_gb = psutil.virtual_memory().total / (1024**3)\n",
        "cpu_count = os.cpu_count() or 2\n",
        "\n",
        "colab_cfg = {\n",
        "    \"memory_limit\": f\"{max(4, int(ram_gb * 0.45))}GB\",\n",
        "    \"threads\": min(cpu_count, 8),\n",
        "    \"model_threads\": min(cpu_count, 16),\n",
        "    \"feature_workers\": max(1, cpu_count // 2 if ram_gb < 20 else cpu_count),\n",
        "    \"max_rss_gb\": round(ram_gb - 2.5, 1),\n",
        "    \"min_free_gb\": 10.0\n",
        "}\n",
        "\n",
        "cfg_path = Path(\"code/business_entity_resolution/configs/colab_auto.json\")\n",
        "cfg_path.write_text(json.dumps(colab_cfg, indent=2))\n",
        "print(f\"Detected: {ram_gb:.1f} GB RAM, {cpu_count} CPUs\")\n",
        "print(\"Adaptive configuration generated:\")\n",
        "print(json.dumps(colab_cfg, indent=2))\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "### 6. Execute Training Workflow Through Tuning\n",
        "This runs the first half of the sequential workflow:\n",
        "1. **Ingest Train**: Country-partitioned Parquet storage.\n",
        "2. **Labels**: Stratified 80/10/10 train/tune/holdout splitting with connected component grouping.\n",
        "3. **Index Train**: Disk-backed SQLite inverted index for all ~10.3M training targets.\n",
        "4. **Candidates Train**: Multi-pass candidate generation for sampled training/tuning S1s.\n",
        "5. **Features Train**: RapidFuzz 58-feature extraction with parallel workers.\n",
        "6. **Train**: LightGBM training with early stopping.\n",
        "7. **Score Train**: Batch scoring on train/tune candidates.\n",
        "8. **Tune**: Exact macro $F_{0.5}$ threshold sweep.\n",
        "9. **Errors**: Detailed failure-mode analysis on false positives and false negatives."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "!python code/business_entity_resolution/run.py run \\\n",
        "    --config code/business_entity_resolution/configs/colab_auto.json \\\n",
        "    --work runs/full \\\n",
        "    --through errors"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "### 7. Inspect Tuning Report & Errors\n",
        "Let's view the optimal macro $F_{0.5}$ threshold and error analysis."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "import json\n",
        "from pathlib import Path\n",
        "tune_path = Path(\"runs/full/reports/tune.json\")\n",
        "if tune_path.exists():\n",
        "    print(json.dumps(json.loads(tune_path.read_text()), indent=2))\n",
        "else:\n",
        "    print(\"tune.json not found yet.\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
